```java
@Service // still a singleton, but now thread-safe
public class CheckoutService {
    // no mutable fields; state stays in the parameter and return value
    public double addItem(double runningTotal, double price) {
        return runningTotal + price; // each call is isolated
    }
}
```
Keeping a singleton stateless is the simplest way to stay thread-safe; reach for prototype only when a bean genuinely needs its own per-use state.

