```java
@Service
public class BillingService {
    private final ObjectProvider<InvoiceGenerator> provider;

    public BillingService(ObjectProvider<InvoiceGenerator> provider) {
        this.provider = provider; // solves the prototype-in-singleton trap
    }

    public byte[] createInvoice() {
        var generator = provider.getObject(); // a fresh instance each call
        return generator.generatePDF();
    }
}
```
ObjectProvider turns the singleton into a factory caller, so each request gets its own prototype instance instead of a shared one.

