@Service // singleton
public class TaskService {
    @Autowired
    private TaskProcessor processor; // one prototype, captured at startup

    public String handle(String task) {
        return processor.process(task); // the same instance for every task
    }
}
```

```java
@Service
public class TaskService {
    private final ObjectProvider<TaskProcessor> provider;

    public TaskService(ObjectProvider<TaskProcessor> provider) {
        this.provider = provider;
    }

    public String handle(String task) {
        return provider.getObject().process(task); // a fresh prototype per task
    }
}
```
ObjectProvider defers lookup to call time, so each task gets its own TaskProcessor instead of a shared one.

